  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_005 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scVI_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 acc, showing that multiprofile + avgpool is a major boost over single-profile. The key open question is whether transformer aggregation can further improve over avgpool for the same encoder/profile setting. config_006 isolates exactly this variable (transformer vs avgpool) while holding RNA encoder (scVI_n200) and profile setting (multiprofile) constant. This is the highest-value next experiment because: (1) it directly exploits the best-performing direction, (2) it cleanly separates the aggregation effect so we know whether to invest remaining budget in transformer-based multimodal configs (config_032/033/038/039) or stick with avgpool, and (3) with only 5 experiments left, resolving this design choice early prevents wasting budget on a suboptimal aggregation strategy across all subsequent multimodal trials."
}

